# `<connector-name>` Marketplace Bundle

This directory contains the Azure Marketplace source artifacts for the
`<connector-name>` connector.

## Contents

- `manifest.yaml` — CNAB bundle manifest.
- `CreateUiDefinition.json` — Azure portal deployment experience.
- `mainTemplate.json` — ARM deployment template.
- `<connector-name>-helm-chart/` — Helm chart containing the
  `AioApplicationDefinition` resource.

## Versions

These values are independently versioned:

- Helm chart: `<chart-version>`
- Application: `<application-version>`
- Marketplace manifest: `<manifest-version>`

## Prerequisites

- Acknowledge that Marketplace deep-copies package images to a public
  Microsoft-managed container registry. Images can be publicly accessible even
  for private plans. Do not package proprietary or sensitive image content that
  must remain private.
- Authenticate to the publishing tenant with Azure CLI.
- Grant the Microsoft packaging service principal `AcrPull` access to the ACR.
- Test the chart in a staging Arc-enabled Kubernetes cluster with Azure IoT
  Operations installed.
- Never place passwords, tokens, client secrets, Docker credentials,
  kubeconfigs, or pull-secret contents in this bundle or support messages.

## Assurance

The generator rendered these source files and ran its local structural checks.
This does not mean the bundle is CPA-verified, Marketplace-validated, approved,
or deployment-validated. Record those states only after the corresponding
external tool or service succeeds and its evidence is retained.

## Definition Classifications

The generated chart uses `applicationSource: Marketplace` and
`applicationType: Connector`. These are required fixed values for this
Marketplace connector chart and must not be changed. The chart rejects other
values and casing variants.

## Validate And Package

Review all generated values, then follow the current Microsoft procedure for
`cpa verify` and `cpa buildbundle`. Use an organization-approved immutable CPA
image digest in a disposable isolated VM or runner with least-privilege,
host-managed authentication. Docker daemon access is host-equivalent privilege;
do not mount the host Docker socket into an unpinned or untrusted image. Require
explicit human approval immediately before building or uploading the package.

## Partner Center Handoff

Assign an owner and completion state for each external item:

- Listing text and media assets
- Support, privacy, and legal URLs or terms
- Availability, pricing, plan, and billing configuration
- Preview audience and certification contacts
- Technical configuration and ACR access
- CPA verification/build evidence
- Marketplace preview ingestion evidence
- Staging installation and AIO reconciliation evidence

Submit the resulting CNAB bundle through Partner Center only after the required
external checks pass. See
[Prepare your Azure container technical assets for a Kubernetes application](https://learn.microsoft.com/partner-center/marketplace-offers/azure-container-technical-assets-kubernetes)
for the complete publication workflow.
